course: dictionary
lesson: 9810
title: A swarm of words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A swarm is a big group moving together, usually insects such as bees, wasps or locusts. «A swarm of locusts can strip whole farms.» Here swarm is a noun, and it names the big group.
explain: Swarm can also be a verb, meaning to move in a large, busy group. «Bees swarmed around the hive.» Swarm can describe people too: a swarm of people is a large crowd moving together.
explain: Look at the words around swarm for clues. In «the beach was swarming with tourists», the word with tells you the beach was full of tourists. Ask yourself what would fit, then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Swarm can be a noun (a swarm) or a verb (to swarm).
fact: «Swarm» means a big group moving together, such as insects flying together.
fact: «Swarming with» means full of something.
fact: «Swarmed» means moved in a large, busy group.
fact: Small words like «with», «of» and «around» are useful context clues.
exercise: «A big locust swarm can eat as much food in a day as millions of people.» What is a locust swarm? | A small fish that lives in rivers | *A large group of locusts flying together | A cloud with no rain | A kind of farm tool
exercise: «In summer the tundra has huge swarms of mosquitoes.» What does swarms mean here? | Single sleepy mosquitoes | *Big groups of mosquitoes | Cold winds blowing over the land | Warm, sunny days
exercise: «Ants swarm and bite the soft inside of an elephant's trunk.» What does swarm mean here? | To fly away alone | To sleep quietly in a tree | *To move in a large, busy group | To grow very tall
test: «The beach was swarming with tourists.» What does swarming with mean? | Empty of tourists | Afraid of tourists | *Full of tourists | Cleaned up for tourists
test: What should you do if you meet a swarm of bees? | *Keep still and walk away calmly | Hit them with a stick | Pick up the swarm and carry it home | Run as fast as you can and wave your arms
exam: «First huge presses squash the steel, then swarms of robot arms join the pieces.» What does swarms of robot arms suggest? | Robot arms that fly away | *Many robot arms working together | One robot arm sleeping in a corner | Robot arms made of wood
